{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Let the earth bring forth grass, herb.</b> דֶּשֶׁא is not a term for עֵשֶׂב, nor is עֵשֶׂב a term for דֶּשֶׁא. And the language of Scripture would not say תַּעֲשִׂיב הָאָרֶץ, for species of grasses are distinct — each on its own is called 'such-and-such עֵשֶׂב,' and a speaker's language would not say 'such-and-such דֶּשֶׁא,' for the term דֶּשֶׁא is the clothing of the earth when it fills with grasses." "<b>Let the earth bring forth grass.</b> Let it fill and be covered with a garment of grasses. In la'az, דֶּשֶׁא is called ארבריץ — all of them mixed together, and every root on its own is called עֵשֶׂב." "<b>Sowing seed.</b> That it grows its seed in it in order to sow from it in another place." "<b>Fruit tree.</b> That the taste of the tree would be like the taste of the fruit. But it did not do so — rather, 'the earth brought forth tree making fruit' and not 'the tree [itself being] fruit.' Therefore, when man was cursed for his sin, it too was punished for its sin and was cursed." "<b>Whose seed is in it.</b> These are the seeds of every fruit from which the tree grows when one plants it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French erbiz / herbes, 'grasses'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:11.031803678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}